  {
   "title": "Operating frequency",
   "body": "Data is 5 bytes (10-byte BCD), little-endian. Digit order: byte-1 low = 10 Hz, byte-1 high = 1 Hz, byte-2 low = 1 kHz, byte-2 high = 100 Hz, byte-3 low = 100 kHz, byte-3 high = 10 kHz, byte-4 low = 10 MHz, byte-4 high = 1 MHz, byte-5 low = 1 GHz (0 fixed), byte-5 high = 100 MHz (0-3 on IC-7610). MAIN/SUB band selection: see command 07.\n\nCommands 00 / 03 / 05 read or set transceive frequency; command 1C 03 reads the transmit frequency in Split.",
   "kind": "panel",
   "pages": [
    10
   ],
   "matches": [
    {
     "cmd": "00",
     "sub_cmd": "",
     "data": ""
    },
