  {
   "title": "Codes for CW message contents",
   "body": "To send CW messages, use the following character codes.\n\nCharacter ASCII code\n0–9     30–39\nA–Z     41–5A\na–z     61–7A\n/         2F\n?         3F\n.         2E\n−         2D\n,         2C\n:         3A\n\nCharacter ASCII code\n’         27\n(         28\n)         29\n=         3D\n+         2B\n”         22\n@         40\nSpace     20\n\nℹ \"FF\" stops sending CW messages.\nℹ \"^\" is used to transmit a string of characters with no inter-character space.",
   "kind": "panel",
   "pages": [
    10
   ],
   "matches": [
    {
     "cmd": "17",
     "sub_cmd": "",
     "data": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Band stacking register",
   "body": "\u0003\u000e\n1 Frequency band codes\nCode Freq. band Frequency range (unit: MHz)\n11 GENE Other than above\n2 Register codes\nCode Registered number\n01 1 (latest)\n03 3 (oldest)\nFor example, when sending/reading the oldest\ncontents in the 21 MHz band, the code “07 03” is\nused.\n",
   "kind": "panel",
   "pages": [
